-- title:
--   Over All Outcomes Reverse Mass Bound Of Not D Add One Le
-- statement:
--   **The reverse mass comparison is harmless when interpolation has too few coordinates.** Let $S$ and $F$ be the strategy and family in the over-all-outcomes construction, let $k$ be a natural number, and let $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta$ be nonnegative errors. Assume the degree parameter satisfies $d+1\not\le k$. Write $M_e$ for expansion mass, $M_p$ for pasted mass, and $E$ for the over-all-outcomes error. Then
--
--   $$
--   d+1\not\le k\quad\Longrightarrow\quad M_e-M_p\le E.
--   $$
--
--   This handles the short-tuple branch of the reverse comparison and avoids a separate interpolation case in later arguments.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.overAllOutcomes_reverse_mass_bound_of_not_d_add_one_le`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
